Causal correlation rules and drift slope calculator.\n  - `modules/profitability.py`: Economic loss breakdown and what-if simulation model.\n  - `utils/constants.py`: Constants, class lists (`crack`, `hole`, `normal`, `rust`, `scratch`), thresholds.\n  - `utils/chart_helpers.py`: Plotly chart factory (waterfall, radar, bar, donut, trend).\n- **Recent Bug Fixes Completed**:\n  - Eliminated `StreamlitDuplicateElementId` by giving all `st.plotly_chart` calls unique keys.\n  - Resolved `cv2.absdiff` NumPy scalar overload error in OpenCV 5.0.\n  - Replaced broken unclosed HTML `div` tags with native `st.container(border=True)` cards.\n  - Removed all emojis from the entire codebase as requested.\n  - Removed all \"NEURAX 3.0\" titles from page title, header, sidebar, report export, and footer.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings & Root Causes\n\n### 1. Model is `yolov8-cls` (Classification), NOT Detection\n- `D:\\acceleration\\best.pt` has `model.task = 'classify'`.\n- Model output contains `result.probs` across 5 classes (`crack`, `hole`, `normal`, `rust`, `scratch`), but `result.boxes` is `None`.\n- **Why Bounding Boxes stopped working**: In the last edit of `compute_gradcam()`, `score.backward()` was called on `output[0, target_class_idx]`. But in PyTorch eval mode or Ultralytics wrappers, model weights or output tensors often have `requires_grad=False`, raising `RuntimeError: element 0 of tensors does not require grad`. The `try...except` block silently caught this and returned `None, []`, causing `bbox` to be `None`!\n- **Solution needed for robust Bounding Boxes**:\n  - Implement a hybrid approach:\n    1. Check if PyTorch Grad-CAM can run with `torch.enable_grad()` and explicit grad tracking on the input tensor.\n    2. Provide a **bulletproof Computer Vision fallback localizer** (`localize_defect_saliency`) using contour detection on the highest-energy region so a localized bounding box is **guaranteed** to be generated whenever the classification is a defect (`crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`), with NO full-image zoom artifact.\n    3. Respect `Display Mode`: `Clean Industrial View`, `Grad-CAM Heatmap`, `Bounding Box`, and `Raw Image`.\n\n### 2. Dataset Ingestion (`Model 2` and `Model 3` .xlsx / .xls)\n- Users have files that can be either `.csv` or `.xlsx` / `.xls` (e.g., `ParametersFile.xls`, `Model 2.xlsx`, `Model 3.csv`).\n- Currently `_upload_csv` in `app.py` has `type=['csv']` and calls `load_csv`.\n- `load_csv()` in `modules/production_analyzer.py` only did `pd.read_csv()`.\n- `Model 3` has 77 columns: alias matching in `production_analyzer.py` must handle complex multi-line naming, extra whitespace, or Excel multi-header/index formats cleanly without throwing exceptions.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- Project root: `C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app`\n- User's local data: `D:\\acceleration\\` (`best.pt`, `Model 1.csv`, `Model 2.csv`, `Model 3.csv`, `ParametersFile.xls`, etc.)\n- Python runtime has all dependencies installed.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Next Steps (Immediate Action Plan)\n\n1. **Fix Bounding Box Engine in `modules/defect_detector.py`**:\n   - Ensure `run_inference` **always** returns a valid, tight bounding box `[x1, y1, x2, y2]` for defective images.\n   - In `compute_gradcam`, wrap in `torch.enable_grad()` and ensure hooks work reliably.\n   - If Grad-CAM fails or produces no contours, immediately fallback to high-precision CV saliency contour bounding box (not covering the whole image).\n   - Ensure `boxed_image` draws the bounding box prominently with target HUD corner brackets and label tag.\n\n2. **Upgrade Dataset Ingestion in `modules/production_analyzer.py` and `app.py`**:\n   - Update `load_dataset` (alias `load_csv`) to accept `.csv`, `.xlsx`, `.xls` seamlessly using `pd.read_excel` (via `openpyxl` / `xlrd`).\n   - In `app.py`, update `file_uploader` to `type=['csv', 'xlsx', 'xls']`.\n   - Ensure `analyze(df)` robustly handles `Model 2` (16 features) and `Model 3` (77 features)